[h1 align=center] A love letter to Podweb

[p- align=center]
Written by saturn91 - a grateful builder living inside Picotron's tiny web.
[-p]

[break height=20]

[h2 align=center] The people behind it all

[grid- columns=auto;auto gap=8]

[h3 align=center] Zep
[h3 align=center] saturn91

[img url=podnet://48932/banner.gfx align=center]
[img url=podnet://48932/banner.gfx align=center]

[p-]
Zep is the creator of PICO-8 and Picotron - the fantasy workstation
this whole world lives in. Without his vision of a cozy, constrained
creative machine, none of this would be possible. Podweb owes its
entire existence to the infrastructure he quietly built.
[-p]

[p-]
saturn91 is the builder of the Podweb browser - the thing you are
reading this in right now. Starting from a simple markup parser and
a handful of Lua, it grew into a proper little web browser running
entirely inside a fantasy workstation. A labour of love for the
community inside Picotron.
[-p]

[-grid]

[break height=20]

[h1 align=center] What is Picotron?

[grid- columns=auto;auto;auto gapX=6 gapY=10]

[h3 align=center] A fantasy workstation
[h3 align=center] Built-in everything
[h3 align=center] Podnet storage

[p-]
Picotron is not just a game console. It is a full fantasy operating
system - complete with file management, a code editor, sprite and
map tools, and a Lua environment. A cozy machine that fits in a
folder on your real computer.
[-p]

[p-]
Sprite editor, map editor, sound tools and a code editor are all
included from day one. Everything a fantasy developer needs to make
games, tools - and apparently a whole web browser - is already
sitting right there waiting.
[-p]

[p-]
Every Lexaloffle user gets cloud storage called podnet. Drop a file
there and it is instantly reachable from anywhere inside Picotron.
Podweb turns that humble file hosting into your own personal page
on a tiny, cozy web.
[-p]

[-grid]

[break height=20]

[h1 align=center] Why I love Podweb

[grid- columns=auto;auto gapX=8 gapY=12]

[h3] It is small
[h3] It is yours

[p-]
No tracking. No ads. No bloated frameworks loading for five seconds
before showing you a paragraph. Just plain text with simple tags,
fetched and rendered inside a fantasy workstation. The web as it
could have been.
[-p]

[p-]
Your podnet space is your space. Write what you like, link to who
you want, and host it all for free with your Lexaloffle account. No
servers to rent, no domain to buy, no deploy pipeline to untangle.
[-p]

[h3] It is connected
[h3] It is growing

[p-]
Webrings, inline links and page navigation let you hop between
users' pages. A real community is slowly forming inside Picotron's
little cloud - artists, developers, and people who just want a
quiet corner of the internet.
[-p]

[p-]
New features keep arriving - images, downloads, comment sections,
webrings, custom fonts, colour themes, and now grid layouts. The
web inside the fantasy machine keeps getting richer, one tag at
a time. And you are already here, exploring it.
[-p]

[-grid]

